* SPDX-License-Identifier: CERN-OHL-P-2.0
* Behavioural models for the ADC input scaler simulations.
* THESE ARE NOT VENDOR MODELS. Each parameter below is either fitted to a
* datasheet number (noted) or an assumption (noted). Results that depend on
* an assumed parameter are flagged in README.md.

* --- BAT54 (one diode of BAT54S), Nexperia BAT54_SER rev 5 ---------------
* IS, N fitted to datasheet MAX VF: 240 mV @ 0.1 mA, 320 mV @ 1 mA
*   -> N = 0.080 V/dec / (2.303*25.85 mV) = 1.34 ; IS = 9.8e-8 A
*   check: 10 mA -> 399 mV (datasheet max 400 mV)
* RS fitted to VF max 800 mV @ 100 mA -> 3.2 ohm
* CJO from Cd max 10 pF @ VR = 1 V (used as CJO; assumption)
* BV = 30 V is the VR rating, used only to keep the model bounded (assumption)
* Reverse current of this model is ~IS (~0.1 uA); NOT fitted to datasheet IR.
.model BAT54 D(IS=9.8e-8 N=1.34 RS=3.2 CJO=10p M=0.5 VJ=0.35 BV=30 IBV=2u)

* --- BZX84-C12, Nexperia BZX84_SER rev 7 ----------------------------------
* VZ 11.40..12.70 V @ IZ = 5 mA; model uses 12.0 V @ 5 mA (mid-range, assumption)
* rdif 25 ohm max @ 5 mA -> RS = 20 (assumption within that limit)
.model BZX84C12 D(IS=1e-14 N=1 RS=20 BV=12.0 IBV=5m CJO=85p)

* --- BSS84, Nexperia BSS84 rev 06 (P-channel) -----------------------------
* VTO = -2.0 V : datasheet MAX |VGS(th)| (worst case for turn-on)
* KP chosen so RDSon = 10 ohm (datasheet max) at VGS = -10 V
*   RDSon ~ 1/(KP*(|VGS|-|VT|)) -> KP = 1/(10*8) = 0.0125 A/V^2
* Gate capacitance: NOT taken from datasheet (not read); 30 pF assumed.
.model BSS84M PMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=-2.0 KP=0.0125 LAMBDA=0.01)

* --- BSS138, onsemi BSS138/D rev 7 (N-channel) ----------------------------
* VTO = 1.5 V : datasheet MAX VGS(th) @ ID = 1 mA (worst case)
* KP so RDSon = 6 ohm (datasheet max) at VGS = 4.5 V -> KP = 1/(6*3) = 0.056
* Ciss 27 pF typ @ VDS = 25 V (datasheet) used as gate-source capacitance
.model BSS138M NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=1.5 KP=0.056 LAMBDA=0.01)

* --- ESP32-S3 ADC pin (assumed protection structure) ----------------------
* The datasheet gives pin capacitance CIN = 2 pF typ and VIH max = VDD+0.3 V.
* The internal protection diodes are NOT specified; a generic silicon diode
* is assumed so the sim can show how fault current splits.
.model ESD_SI D(IS=1e-14 N=1.0 RS=10)
